  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f$ and $g$ be two positive valued functions defined on $[-1,1]$, such that $f(-x)=1/f(x)$ and $g$ is an even function with $\\int_{-1}^{1}g(x)\\,dx=1$. Then $I=\\int_{-1}^{1}f(x)g(x)\\,dx$ satisfies",
  "options": {
    "A": "$I\\ge1$",
    "B": "$I\\le1$",
    "C": "$\\frac13<I<3$",
    "D": "$I=1$"
  },
  "answer": "A",
